==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
Referring to the character in the novel ''{{w|Uncle Tom's Cabin}}''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[uncle|Uncle]] [[Tom]]}}

# {{lb|en|pejorative|offensive|ethnic slur}} A [[black]] [[man]] who is [[servile]] towards [[white]] [[authority]] and [[accepting]] of [[white supremacy]], a [[black]] [[race traitor]].
#: {{syn|en|coconut|Oreo|coon}}
#* {{RQ:Harper's|year=1968|author=w:Norman Mailer|title=Nixon in Miami|section=§6
|passage=...their master... was no ad for anybody but the most arcane Black Power, he was an old prince of a [[witch doctor]]&mdash;insult him at your peril&mdash;but the other ten musicians with their trumpets and snares and assorted brass would prove no pull for {{w|Richard Nixon|Nixon}} on TV with any Black votes watching, for they were old and meek, naught but elderly Black Southern musicians, a veritable [[Ganges]] of '''Uncle Toms'''. They had disappeared with {{w|Tom Swift}} and {{w|Little Lord Fauntleroy}}.}}

